ncing (ELB)","description":"Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#networking-content-dev","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Networking \u0026 Content Delivery","description":"Networking \u0026 Content Delivery","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#cloudfront","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon CloudFront","description":"Amazon CloudFront","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:01:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:22+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#infrastructure","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Infrastructure","description":"Infrastructure","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:32:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-19T04:21:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#industry#travel-and-hospitality","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#industry","name":"travel-and-hospitality","description":"\u003cp\u003eAs of 4/2023, this tag is initially being used specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/travel-and-hospitality/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can switch to the AND operator, enabling them to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2019-07-17T22:21:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:41:02+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#smb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","description":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#aws-case-study-polljoy","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"aws-case-study-polljoy","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:50:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:40+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Startup polljoy aims to improve ratings for mobile applications in app marketplaces. The firm is running its web services, software development kit, and databases in AWS. This has enabled polljoy to achieve 99.999 percent infrastructure availability while supporting more than 1,000 user requests per second during peak periods.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/logos/customers/polljoy-logo.2a266b1cd4eda565c7967feab308ad315762474a.png","displayLocation":"Hong Kong","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eStartup polljoy aims to improve ratings for mobile applications in app marketplaces. The firm is running its web services, software development kit, and databases in AWS. This has enabled polljoy to achieve 99.999 percent infrastructure availability while supporting more than 1,000 user requests per second during peak periods.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Software \u0026 Internet","sortDate":"2015-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/polljoy/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"polljoy","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2015","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"AWS Case Study: polljoy"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#compute","locale":